<title>SOUTH KOREA: Two S.Korean firms buy 21,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Two S.Korean firms buy 21,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Cheil Jedang Corp and Dongah Flour Mills Co Ltd on Wednesday bought a total of 21,000 tonnes of U.S. No.1 wheat from Japanese trading house Marubeni Corp, traders said.  </p>
<p>Cheil Jedang bought 11,000 tonnes at basis over May futures on the U.S grain futures markets including the Chicago Board of Trade, traders said. Shipment was set for April 10-May 10 to the western port of Inchon.</p>
<p>Dongah Flour bought the remaining 10,000 tonnes at fixed prices.</p>
<p>Details are as follows:</p>
<p>Cheiljedang Corp</p>
<p>  TYPE OF WHEAT	   TONNE   PRICE/BUSHEL (FOB)</p>
<p>  Soft White		3,500   $0.4350 (over CBOT's May)</p>
<p>(protein max 10.0%)</p>
<p>  Hard Red Winter	 4,500   $0.8500 (over KCBT's May)</p>
<p>  Dark Northern Spring  3,000   $1.1600 (over MGE's May)</p>
<p>Dongah Flour Mills Co Ltd</p>
<p>  TYPE OF WHEAT	   TONNE   PRICE/TONNE (FOB)</p>
<p>  Soft White		3,000   $154.43</p>
<p>(protein max 10.0%)</p>
<p>  Soft White		2,000   $152.49</p>
<p>(protein max 9.5%)</p>
<p>  Hard Red Winter	 4,000   $179.40</p>
<p>  Dark Northern Spring  1,000   $181.45</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
